# Line endings are decided here rather than by whatever each clone happens to
# have in its local git config. Without this file a clone with core.autocrlf set
# to true checks tracked text out with CRLF, which changes the bytes a checksum
# was computed over and the bytes a fixture parser reads. That failure is silent
# on the machine where it happens and shows up as a stopped run on somebody
# else's.
#
# text=auto lets git detect text and leave anything it detects as binary alone.
# eol=lf fixes the checked-out ending, so the working tree matches what is
# stored and a round trip through a checkout changes nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose bytes are the artefact rather than a rendering of it. Named
# explicitly instead of left to detection, because detection is a heuristic and
# these are the files where being wrong costs a checksum.
*.json text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
fixtures/checksums.txt text eol=lf

# Diff hunks read better with the enclosing definition named.
*.py diff=python
*.md diff=markdown
